  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "No prior evidence exists, so the priority is establishing a strong, interpretable baseline. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest canonical configuration: it uses the most standard RNA encoder (PCA-2000), the simplest profile setting, and avoids confounding from image, aggregation, or fusion choices. This gives a clean reference accuracy for RNA-only performance. In subsequent experiments I can then test image_only (config_010) and multimodal (config_016) with the same PCA-2000 encoder to isolate the marginal contribution of each modality and of fusion, while keeping the RNA representation fixed. Starting from the simplest model avoids the risk of over-crediting complexity and provides the anchor against which all later gains (or losses) are measured—critical when only 10 experiments are available."
}

